  "body": "This ports over the content and IDL attribute definitions, as well as\nthe `<meta http-equiv>`, from the Referrer Policy specification. In the\nprocess, it clarifies several things that document did not:\n- Conformance requirements for authors\n- It's http-equiv, not name, for the `<meta>` attribute\n- The missing and invalid value defaults are a special state in which\n  the policy is inherited from the document. (There's more work to do\n  in making this explicit.)\n\nThere is more work to do; see especially:\n- https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-referrer-policy/issues/40\n- https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-referrer-policy/issues/30\n\nThis closes https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-referrer-policy/issues/27.\n\n/cc @jeisinger @estark37\n",
